# Base URL of the Hothobs API, including the /api prefix.
# Local development runs the backend from ../hothobs-backend on port 4000.
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:4000/api

# ── Payment (Paystack) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# There is NO Paystack key to set here, and there should never be one.
# Checkout is a server-side redirect flow: POST /orders returns an
# authorization URL, the browser leaves the site for Paystack's own page,
# and Paystack sends the customer back to /order/complete, which asks the
# API to verify the reference. No card details and no Paystack credentials
# ever touch this app, so it needs neither a public nor a secret key.
#
# What does have to line up lives in ../hothobs-backend/.env:
#
#   SITE_URL      must be this site's public origin — it is what Paystack
#                 redirects back to. Locally http://localhost:5173; in
#                 production the real domain (e.g. https://hothobscuisines.com).
#                 Get it wrong and paying customers land on the wrong host.
#   CORS_ORIGIN   must include that same origin, or the browser will block
#                 every API call this app makes.
#   PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY  and the dashboard webhook pointing at
#                 <API origin>/api/payments/webhook — that webhook is what
#                 confirms an order when the customer closes the tab before
#                 being redirected back.
#
# So VITE_API_URL above is the only Paystack-relevant setting on this side:
# it must reach the same backend whose SITE_URL points here.
